# A name a held definition requires, which no one can give and nothing types, is refused at the call that
# starts the chain, as when a type is known (unit_held_call_required_input_unavailable_refused): one admission
# rule for an input with a type and one without (DORMANT-BODY-FREE-INPUT).  r reads zz; the unit does not
# declare it.  The definition f calls r and only hands zz on; inner calls the held f and has no zz.  The root
# calls inner and has none either: that call is refused.
fn: r () int
    return: zz + 1
end: r

fn: mk (int: k) fn: () int
    fn: f () int
        return: k + r()
    return: f

@: u0 mk(5)

fn: inner () int
    return: u0()
end: inner

int: a inner()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
